                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I didn't find this satisfying as either a card game or a KB/HoMM-like.  This isn't a TCG RPG as with the old M:tG game by Microprose.  You \"build\" a \"deck,\" but the spells available to you are extremely limited and story-gated, and the deck itself is only 16 cards.  Each enemy encounter basically requires a specific deck build to defeat, but there's no way to save and load different decks, so you'll be doing this manually every time - to the extent that you're able with the very small selection of cards that you have.  Battles themselves can also take ages, often because enemies have so many highly effective ways to shut down your offense, heal themselves, or both.  Stalemates are so commonplace that a special mechanic was added just to break them.  There were a number of fights that I won simply by outlasting my opponent while sudden death ticked down, since neither of us could damage the other.\n\nThe game probably becomes more interesting later on as more tactical options open up, but after playing through several missions over six hours, I'm just not compelled to continue.",
